v 3
d 'HMBIVPOIS': module to fit hidden Markov bivariate Poisson regression for panel counts
d
d hmbivpois fits the hidden Markov bivariate Poisson regression of
d Laudicella and Li Donni (2022, Journal of Applied Econometrics 37: 521-536)
d to two counts observed on the same individuals over time. Given a latent
d state that follows a first-order Markov chain, the two counts have Poisson
d margins whose means depend on regressors, on the lagged counts and on the
d state. The dependence between the two counts is the Famoye form, the Frank
d copula or the normal copula. Estimation is by the EM algorithm followed by
d direct maximization. Postestimation: predict (means, posterior probabilities,
d Viterbi path, joint probabilities) and estat (ic, transition, lrtrans,
d stability, ame).
d
d KW: hidden Markov
d KW: latent Markov
d KW: bivariate Poisson
d KW: count data
d KW: panel data
d KW: copula
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Author: Paolo Li Donni
d Support: https://github.com/plidonni/hmbivpois
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261118
d
f hmbivpois.ado
